{"availability":"available","full":"Mohammed-Taysser/officehut","name":"officehut","description":"A small, paper-flavoured UI kit for dashboards and back-office apps. Plain CSS + tiny vanilla JS, with typed React bindings.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T05:13:12Z","updated":"2026-10-08T05:52:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://officehut.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://officehut.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:49:05.495Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:49:05.495Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:49:05.495Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:52.584Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:28:38.593Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T15:49:05.495Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Quiet, papery UI for the screens people use all day.","A small UI kit for dashboards and back-office apps — invoices, rotas, tickets, approvals —","dressed like a school exercise book left on an office desk."],"features":["Plain CSS first. Every component works with class names alone. JavaScript is only for things HTML can't do yet.","The same markup everywhere. The React components render exactly the classes you'd write by hand, so you can mix server-rendered HTML and React on one page.","Its own look. A school exercise book on an office desk — see The school identity below. No gradients, no glass, no stock-template feel.","Built for long sessions. 14px base text, tabular numbers, a \"night shift\" theme, a compact density, and right-to-left support out of the box."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Mohammed-Taysser/officehut/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"40b372ca5b9518723911507fe1b938746cb5e118e1cf16bf2c98caeb2171d381","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:52.755Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:52.755Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Quiet, papery UI for the sc